# MTG retrieval data source

Card data lives in **Neon Postgres + pgvector**, populated weekly by a separate repo (`mtg-db`).
Full contract: `apps/ai_mtg_search/docs/neon-pgvector-handoff.md` — read it before changing retrieval.

Slang / labeling taxonomy is `apps/ai_mtg_search/data/taxonomy.json`.
`mtg_taxonomy.py` only loads it. Do not grow a second tree.

## Hard invariants

- **Read-only.** This app never writes to `cards` or `embeddings`, and never downloads MTGJson/rules data. `mtg-db` owns all document vectors; this app embeds **queries only**.
- **Embedding model must match:** `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, **384-dim**, cosine. Never use OpenAI embeddings (1536-dim) against these vectors.
- Similarity is `1 - (embedding <=> qvec)`; order by `embedding <=> qvec`.

## Schema essentials

- `cards`: PK `(scryfall_oracle_id, face_index)`, one row per face. `TEXT[]` columns (`colors`, `color_identity`, `types`, `subtypes`, `keywords`) are GIN-indexed; `legalities` is JSONB.
- `embeddings`: PK `(id, source, chunk_index)`. `source` is one of `card_name` | `card_text` | `rules`.
- Card embedding ids are `"{scryfall_oracle_id}:{face_index}"`; join with
  `ON c.scryfall_oracle_id = split_part(e.id,':',1) AND c.face_index = split_part(e.id,':',2)::int`.

## Retrieval gotchas

- `card_text` vectors contain **preprocessed oracle text only** — no name, type line, mana cost, or P/T. Filter those with SQL on `cards`, not with the vector.
- ~366 `card_text` rows have empty `chunk_text`; always add `AND length(e.chunk_text) > 0`.
- Preprocess queries with `preprocess_oracle_text` when they contain mana/tap symbols like `{T}` or `{W/P}`.
- Prefer filter-then-vector composition over stuffing metadata into one blob.
- Neon scales to zero, so the first query after idle is slow. If recall looks off on IVFFlat, raise `ivfflat.probes` per session.
